---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import { LINKS } from '../config';
import pkg from '../../../package.json';
const browsers = [
  { name: 'Chrome', icon: '/chrome.png', store: 'Chrome Web Store', url: LINKS.chromeStore },
  { name: 'Firefox', icon: '/firefox.png', store: 'Firefox Add-ons', url: LINKS.firefoxAddons },
];
---
<Doc title="Install RoFit" lead="RoFit is coming to the Chrome Web Store and Firefox Add-ons. You can try it now in the site demo or build it from GitHub." toc={false}>
  <div class="stores" aria-label="Browser stores">
    {browsers.map((browser) => (
      <article class="store">
        <img src={browser.icon} alt="" width="56" height="56" />
        <div><strong>{browser.name}</strong><span>{browser.store}</span></div>
        {browser.url
          ? <a class="btn btn-curtain" href={browser.url}>Add to {browser.name}</a>
          : <button type="button" class="btn" disabled aria-label={browser.name + ' coming soon'}>Coming soon</button>}
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>
  <div class="install-meta" data-release-version={pkg.version}><a href="/#demo">Try the demo</a><a href={LINKS.github}>View on GitHub</a><p id="detect" role="status" hidden></p></div>
  <h2>Load it from source</h2>
  <p>You need Node.js and Git. RoFit has no accounts and needs no keys.</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Get the code from <a href={LINKS.github} rel="noopener">the GitHub repository</a> (download it as a ZIP, or <code>git clone</code>).</li>
    <li>In that folder, run <code>npm ci</code>, then <code>npm run build</code>. On Windows you can double-click <code>setup.bat</code> instead; it does both and walks you through the next step.</li>
    <li>Open <code>chrome://extensions</code> and switch on <strong>Developer mode</strong> (top right).</li>
    <li>Choose <strong>Load unpacked</strong> and pick the <code>dist</code> folder that the build created.</li>
    <li>Open any profile on roblox.com. Use the <strong>Saved Outfits</strong> row or <strong>Outfits</strong> tab.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Chrome may remind you at startup about developer-mode extensions. That is normal for anything not installed from the store.</p>

  <h2>Check what you installed</h2>
  <p>On <code>chrome://extensions</code>, open RoFit’s <em>Details</em> and look at <em>Permissions</em> and <em>Site access</em>. They should match the <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a> exactly: Roblox’s six read-only API hosts, plus storage, a daily cleanup alarm and the active tab.</p>

  <h2 id="update">Updating and removing</h2>
  <p>Updates from source are manual: pull the new code, rebuild in the same folder to preserve your library, then press the reload icon on RoFit’s card. To remove it, use <em>Remove</em> on the same card; that also deletes everything RoFit stored.</p>

  <h2>Trouble?</h2>
  <p>See the <a href="/guides/no-outfits">guide on profiles with no outfits</a> or the <a href="/support">support page</a>.</p>
</Doc>

<script>import '../app.ts';</script>
<style>
  .stores { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 14px; margin-bottom: 22px; }
  .store { min-width: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; align-items: center; gap: 14px; padding: clamp(16px, 3vw, 24px); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 20px; background: linear-gradient(150deg, var(--paper), var(--wall-2)); }
  .store img { display: block; object-fit: contain; width: 56px; height: 56px; }
  .store strong, .store span { display: block; }
  .store strong { font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .store span { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: .86rem; }
  .store .btn { grid-column: 1 / -1; min-height: 44px; justify-content: center; }
  .store button { background: var(--wall); color: var(--ink-2); cursor: default; }
  .install-meta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 20px; align-items: center; }
  .install-meta :global(.detect) { flex-basis: 100%; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: .9rem; }
  @media (max-width: 540px) { .stores { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
